  "findings": [
    "Three initial workers configure the selected structure through25b68/28b80, clear its byte1, then call1f354->1d488. Fourth worker1d480 immediately returns.",
    "24 setup calls have constant field indices; computed writes stay within the230hex-byte selected structure and do not reach its callback-table pointer+22c. 1d554 pair writes range+15c..+1db under its32-entry loop. These are local bounds, not whole-callee closure.",
    "1d488 loads pointer[P+22c], then callback from that table indexed by state bytesP+1f/P+20, bounded locally by byteP+21. Therefore command41 has a second data-dependent callback layer before the final pointer reload/store.",
    "All four initial structures have zero step0 state/cursor/start/end and callback0=1d7fc, an immediate-return function. This describes image initialization only, not actual command-time contents.",
    "Final store1d7e2 still rereads global15874 after callbacks. Stability across runtime callbacks, helper1d538/error path, synchronization and other writers remains unproved."
  ],
  "next": "Trace initialization/runtime writers of P+22c and state bytes+1f/+20/+21, and reachable second-level callbacks before claiming final pointer preservation or a CC connection.",
